\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{The representation carried by both odd fields}
\date{2026-11-19}

\p{The bilinear in \ref{fdip-011P} uses one fermion module and
its dual. Its onsite coefficients are specified by a linear
equivariant map. This vector-like coupling gives no separate
left and right representations. The quantities #{m+y} and
#{m-y} in \ref{fdip-011O} are eigenvalues of an onsite
endomorphism. A particle mass would require independent spectral
and dynamical information.}

\p{\citet{authors’ preprint, §5.3, pp. 31–33}{frohlich1981higgs}
discuss a mass matrix for invariant fields with trivial residual
group. Their example on p. 33 with a residual circle uses
different representations for a left doublet and a right singlet.
Those representation data are additional inputs to that physical
comparison.}
